{"name":"Light Quilt","hex":"#fde1d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"quilt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bed covering consisting of two layers of fabric stitched together, with insulation between, often having a decorative design.","A roll of material with sound-absorbing properties, used in soundproofing."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To construct a quilt.","To construct something, such as clothing, using the same technique."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quilt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quilt","blocks":[{"text":"A quilt is a multi-layered textile, traditionally composed of two or more layers of fabric or fiber. Commonly three layers are used with a filler material. These layers traditionally include a woven cloth top, a layer of batting or wadding, and a woven back combined using the techniques of quilting. This is the process of sewing on the face of the fabric, and not just the edges, to combine the three layers together to reinforce the material. Stitching patterns can be a decorative element. A single piece of fabric can be used for the top of a quilt, but in many cases the top is created from smaller fabric pieces joined, or patchwork. The pattern and color of these pieces creates the design. Quilts may contain valuable historical information about their creators, \"visualizing particular segments of history in tangible, textured ways\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Russellquilter.jpg/330px-Russellquilter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quilt","wikidata":"Q1064538"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/%22New_York_Beauty%22.jpg/500px-%22New_York_Beauty%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/%22New_York_Beauty%22.jpg/1280px-%22New_York_Beauty%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/%22New_York_Beauty%22.jpg/500px-%22New_York_Beauty%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pieced quilt, cottons, c. 1865, unknown maker, Kentucky, dimensions: 80×85 inches. The design had numerous names such as Rocky Road and Crown of Thorns until it was renamed and marketed as \"New York Beauty\" in the 1930s by the Mountain Mist company. Included in the book \"New York Beauty, Quilts from the Volckening Collection\" (Quiltmania, France). Collection of Bill Volckening, Portland, Oregon.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%22New_York_Beauty%22.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/